[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3794057435","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115319#issuecomment-3794057435","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115319","id":3794057435,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iJLjb","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-24T07:26:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-24T07:26:34Z","body":"This is one example of why complex inline statements in indentation-based languages ​​can be confusing and should be avoided. Here's another example:\n\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/6924\n\nPython disallows blocks within inline blocks; `if 1: if 2: print(3)` will cause a syntax error even without an `else` clause.\n\nFor GDScript, I think we should disallow any potentially confusing inline statements (blocks within inline blocks, multiple statements separated by semicolons within an inline block). But this would be considered a compatibility break, so it's likely only possible in 5.0.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3794057435/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3794163366","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115319#issuecomment-3794163366","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115319","id":3794163366,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iJlam","user":{"login":"addmix","id":38119387,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MTE5Mzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38119387?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix","html_url":"https://github.com/addmix","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addmix/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-24T07:59:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-24T07:59:25Z","body":"I would agree, this format is bad practice, and almost entirely unnecessary, however I think it's still reasonable to fix how the association of the else statement is interpreted.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3794163366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},